ated as if  natural immunity  it does not exist that is ultimately i  think one of the great failures of our  medical leadership  is ignoring natural immunity which  changes everything  you know i'm wondering then how do  people get it twice  well look we know breakthrough  infections happen after vaccinated  immunity  they're rare and they're mild that's the  same with natural immunity in the giant  study in denmark it was six tenths of  one percent and presumably most of those  cases are mild  just because somebody tests positive  does not mean we've got a health problem  the pcr test  can detect as few as 10 molecules of  viral particles in your nose  that doesn't mean you have the infection  it may mean your immune system worked to  fend off the infection  yeah maybe trying to do some things we  didn't though too because remember they  started testing people  on the opposite ends not their nose but  but uh  their bums if you will just to be  delicate because it's 11 a.m eastern  dr fauci and cdc head director wolinski  say  they understand why people are afraid to  remove their masks  you can understand that when people have  been following  a certain trend for a considerable  period of time that it may take time for  them to adjust  not everybody is going to feel like it's  time to rip off their masks for 16  months we've been saying that it's  important to wear these masks to protect  yourselves and now what we're saying is  um it's going to be hard to get back to  um to you know life as we knew it  without these masks  you know i'm old enough to remember  because it's only been a few months  uh when dr fauci said on 60 minutes  overtime that's the online version of 60  minutes  you watch it a little bit when the  show's over and sometimes you get little  drips like  well masks aren't the really end-all  be-all i mean i remember when he was not  really encouraging people  to to wear masks maybe the mixed  messaging played a role  in all of this people's percep